Summary: Implemented Phase 1 isotropic material support with typed `Medium`/`PECMedium`/`PMCMedium` models, typed IR lowering, coefficient compilation, scene material sampling, and constitutive update helpers plus tests, docs, and an example.
Key findings:
- `autofdtd.materials` now exposes validated isotropic public models and normalization via `medium_model_from_value()`.
- `autofdtd.ir` lowers supported isotropic media into typed `MediumIR`, `PECMediumIR`, and `PMCMediumIR` instead of generic medium envelopes.
- `autofdtd.compiler.materials` compiles lossy-isotropic Yee coefficients and represents PEC/PMC as explicit clamp-zero constitutive modes.
- `autofdtd.kernels.materials` provides staged electric and magnetic constitutive update helpers with a NumPy path and optional Warp-availability reporting.
- Scene-level material application is now test-covered through point sampling and compiled-coefficient attachment across background and structure precedence.
- Verification passed with `pytest -q` (65 passed) and `ruff check src tests`.
Follow-up: Warp is not installed in this environment, so the constitutive runtime path is currently exercised through the NumPy helper while preserving an explicit optional-Warp seam for later GPU kernel work.
Reported artifacts:
- /workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/materials/isotropic.py: Typed Phase 1 isotropic material models and coercion helpers.
- /workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/compiler/materials.py: Isotropic coefficient compilation and scene material sampling utilities.
- /workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/kernels/materials.py: Constitutive update helpers and backend metadata for isotropic material paths.
- /workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py: Typed isotropic medium IR models and lowering integration.
- /workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_materials.py: Serialization, validation, scene application, coefficient, IR, and constitutive-update coverage for isotropic materials.
- /workspace/autofdtd/docs/materials.md: Material-scope documentation for the new baseline isotropic family.
