p, auxiliary-state updates, and existing isotropic paths."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/materials.md","description":"Material documentation updated for PoleResidue support and runtime-state behavior."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"The current PoleResidue runtime path is an explicit electric-dispersive auxiliary-state update built around one complex polarization accumulator per pole. Later Lorentz/Drude/Debye/Sellmeier tasks should reuse this coefficient and state contract where possible instead of introducing competing layouts.","next_action":"none"}
