{"task_id":"task-022","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented `StablePML` and `Absorber` boundary support across the public API, typed IR, boundary compiler, staged runtime path, examples, docs, and representative absorption tests.","key_findings":["`StablePML` and `Absorber` are now first-class public boundary edges with Tidy3D-aligned defaults, explicit `Boundary` / `BoundarySpec` constructors, and zero-dimension coercion behavior shared with baseline `PML`.","Boundary IR now distinguishes `PML`, `StablePML`, and `Absorber` through typed payloads (`PMLIR`, `StablePMLIR`, `AbsorberIR`) plus family-specific axis and face metadata on `BoundarySpecIR`.","Runtime compilation keeps the existing staged damping-layer seam: `StablePML` lowers onto the baseline PML coefficient path with a separate profile tag, while `Absorber` lowers into conductivity-only attenuation coefficients with a reflective outer-wall policy.","The absorbing-boundary runtime and state allocator now handle all three absorbing families through the shared staged kernel path, while kernel metadata advertises explicit `stable_pml` and `absorber` mode support.","Focused verification passed with `PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q tests/test_boundaries.py tests/test_ir.py tests/test_imports.py tests/test_containers.py` and `PYTHONPATH=src python -m compileall src/autofdtd`."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/boundaries/models.py","description":"Added `AbsorberParams`, `StablePML`, `Absorber`, and public constructors for the new absorbing boundary families."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/compiler/boundaries.py","description":"Extended absorbing-boundary compilation to prepare StablePML and Absorber coefficient profiles and per-family face metadata."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/kernels/boundaries.py","description":"Extended staged boundary kernels to handle StablePML and Absorber runtime modes."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/runtime/boundaries.py","description":"Updated runtime state allocation so all absorbing families share the staged boundary execution path."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Added typed IR lowering for `StablePML`, `Absorber`, and `AbsorberParams`."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_boundaries.py","description":"Added representative tests for StablePML and Absorber compilation, IR lowering, state allocation, reflective ghost behavior, and staged absorption."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/boundaries.md","description":"Updated boundary-scope documentation to cover the implemented absorbing-boundary subset and current limits."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-022-attempt-001/result.json","description":"Structured task result for this loop iteration."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"The current `StablePML` implementation is a preset-driven extension of the staged PML backend, and `Absorber` is a conductivity-ramp subset with a reflective outer wall. `task-023` should build ABC-family behavior on the existing absorbing-face metadata without redesigning the shared staged boundary seam.","next_action":"none"}
diff --git a/docs/boundaries.md b/docs/boundaries.md
index 70ff9c0b0ce36fcafedd208cfd5a16ad29a5e0c0..43156dc89a37e90f03b4dacff0da3489f32e2a25
--- a/docs/boundaries.md
+++ b/docs/boundaries.md
@@ -1,36 +1,53 @@
 # Boundary Scope
 
-Phase 1 now has an explicit non-absorbing boundary surface built around
-`Periodic`, `PECBoundary`, `PMCBoundary`, `Boundary`, and `BoundarySpec`.
+Phase 1 now has an explicit boundary surface for non-absorbing, phase-aware, and
+absorbing edges built around `Periodic`, `BlochBoundary`, `PECBoundary`,
+`PMCBoundary`, `PML`, `StablePML`, `Absorber`, `Boundary`, and `BoundarySpec`.
 
 ## Public API
 
-- `Periodic`, `PECBoundary`, and `PMCBoundary` are typed boundary-edge models.
+- `Periodic`, `BlochBoundary`, `PECBoundary`, `PMCBoundary`, `PML`, `StablePML`,
+  and `Absorber` are typed boundary-edge models.
 - `Boundary` pairs `minus` and `plus` edges along one axis.
 - `BoundarySpec` carries `x`, `y`, and `z` axis boundaries and defaults to periodic
   behavior on all sides in the currently implemented subset.
 - If a periodic edge is placed opposite a PEC or PMC edge, the periodic edge is
   coerced to the conductor edge with a warning so later runtime handling stays
   reflection-based instead of mixing halo semantics on one axis.
+- `StablePML` keeps the same parameter surface as `PML` but uses a more conservative
+  default preset.
+- `Absorber` uses a simpler conductivity-only profile and defaults
+  `extrude_structures=False`, matching the local Tidy3D schema surface.
 
 ## Lowering And Runtime
 
 - `autofdtd.ir` lowers the supported subset into typed `PeriodicIR`,
-  `PECBoundaryIR`, `PMCBoundaryIR`, `BoundaryIR`, and `BoundarySpecIR` payloads.
+  `BlochBoundaryIR`, `PECBoundaryIR`, `PMCBoundaryIR`, `PMLIR`, `StablePMLIR`,
+  `AbsorberIR`, `BoundaryIR`, and `BoundarySpecIR` payloads.
 - `autofdtd.compiler.boundaries.compile_boundary_spec()` turns the public boundary
   surface into a runtime plan with explicit per-face mode tags, sign transforms,
-  halo depth, and stage ordering.
+  halo depth, stage ordering, and per-face absorbing profile metadata.
 - `autofdtd.kernels.boundaries.apply_boundary_ghosts()` applies the compiled plan to
   vector fields with one ghost cell on each side.
 - Periodic boundaries copy ghost cells from the opposite interior face.
+- Bloch boundaries apply explicit complex phase factors on wrapped ghost values.
 - PEC and PMC boundaries use reflection-sign conventions so tangential-versus-normal
   field parity is explicit instead of being hidden in a monolithic timestep kernel.
+- `PML` and `StablePML` share the staged damping-layer backend and differ through
+  compiled coefficient presets.
+- `Absorber` uses the same staged region-update seam but with conductivity-only
+  attenuation coefficients and a reflective outer wall.
 
 ## Current Limits
 
-- Runtime compilation currently supports only the non-absorbing subset:
-  `Periodic`, `PECBoundary`, `PMCBoundary`, `Boundary`, and `BoundarySpec`.
-- `BlochBoundary`, `PML`, `StablePML`, `Absorber`, and ABC-family boundaries remain
-  outside the runtime compiler path for this task and fail explicitly there.
+- Runtime compilation currently supports `Periodic`, `BlochBoundary`,
+  `PECBoundary`, `PMCBoundary`, `PML`, `StablePML`, `Absorber`, `Boundary`, and
+  `BoundarySpec`.
+- `StablePML` is currently implemented as a preset-driven extension of the baseline
+  staged PML backend rather than a separate split-field formulation.
+- `Absorber` is currently implemented as a conductivity-ramp absorbing subset with a
+  reflective outer wall, not a full material-aware adiabatic absorber.
+- ABC-family boundaries remain outside the runtime compiler path and should fail
+  explicitly until `task-023`.
 - The kernel helpers assume vector fields shaped `(nx, ny, nz, 3)` with one ghost
   cell per face.
