phase1/runs/task-019-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:116820:{"task_id":"task-019","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented the foundational non-absorbing boundary surface across the public API, typed IR, compiler/runtime metadata, ghost-update kernels, tests, and docs.","key_findings":["The public API now has typed `Periodic`, `PECBoundary`, `PMCBoundary`, `Boundary`, and `BoundarySpec` models, with periodic-opposite-conductor coercion to keep each axis on one runtime mode.","Boundary lowering is now typed in IR via `PeriodicIR`, `PECBoundaryIR`, `PMCBoundaryIR`, `BoundaryIR`, and `BoundarySpecIR`, while unsupported boundary families still fall back to the generic boundary envelope.","`compile_boundary_spec()` now produces explicit per-face halo metadata and reflection parity, and the runtime/kernel path can apply periodic copy plus PEC/PMC ghost-cell transforms on `(nx, ny, nz, 3)` vector fields.","Unsupported runtime compilation is explicit: PML, Bloch, and ABC-family boundaries are still parseable at the API layer but rejected by the Phase 1 non-absorbing boundary compiler.","Focused verification passed: `PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q tests/test_boundaries.py tests/test_containers.py tests/test_ir.py tests/test_imports.py tests/test_planning.py` and `PYTHONPATH=src python -m compileall src`. `ruff` was not installed in the environment."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/boundaries/models.py","description":"Typed non-absorbing boundary public models and normalization helpers."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/compiler/boundaries.py","description":"Boundary runtime compilation metadata for periodic, PEC, and PMC halo handling."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/kernels/boundaries.py","description":"Concrete ghost-cell update helpers and boundary kernel metadata."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/runtime/boundaries.py","description":"Runtime wrapper that applies compiled boundary ghost updates."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Typed boundary IR classes and lowering helpers."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_boundaries.py","description":"Focused tests for boundary normalization, IR lowering, compiler/runtime behavior, and explicit unsupported-boundary errors."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/boundaries.md","description":"Boundary scope documentation for the implemented Phase 1 subset."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-019-attempt-001/result.json","description":"Structured task result matching the Phase 1 output schema."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"The supported runtime subset is intentionally narrow for this task. `task-020` and later boundary tasks should extend the compiled boundary metadata and ghost-update stage instead of redesigning the public boundary containers.","next_action":"none"}

