phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-018/codex.stdout.txt:147:- `src/autofdtd/materials/dispersive.py` now provides a Phase 1 `PoleResidue` public model with JSON-safe complex-pair storage, causal validation (`Re(a) <= 0`), `eps_model()`, and limited `Medium` conversion helpers.
phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-018/codex.stdout.txt:155:- `src/autofdtd/compiler/materials.py` now compiles `Lorentz`, `Drude`, and `Debye` by first reducing them to equivalent `PoleResidue` terms, re-tagging the compiled coefficients with the public family name, and failing explicitly when converted poles are too stiff for the current exact-hold timestep path.
phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-018/codex.stdout.txt:181:- Phase 1 `Sellmeier` support is intentionally passive-only and homogeneous-only: `B_i >= 0`, `C_i >= 0`, zero-`C_i` terms fold into `eps_inf`, and all timestep execution reuses the existing electric-only `PoleResidueMaterialCoefficients` path instead of creating a new auxiliary-state layout.
