phase1/runs/task-021-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:92068:- `src/autofdtd/grid/subpixel.py` now provides the first explicit subpixel policy layer with `SubpixelSpec`, `Staircasing`, and `PolarizedAveraging`, plus Tidy3D-style `bool` coercion for `Simulation.subpixel`.
phase1/runs/task-021-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:92073:- `src/autofdtd/materials/dispersive.py` now provides a Phase 1 `PoleResidue` public model with JSON-safe complex-pair storage, causal validation (`Re(a) <= 0`), `eps_model()`, and limited `Medium` conversion helpers.
phase1/runs/task-021-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:92081:- `src/autofdtd/compiler/materials.py` now compiles `Lorentz`, `Drude`, and `Debye` by first reducing them to equivalent `PoleResidue` terms, re-tagging the compiled coefficients with the public family name, and failing explicitly when converted poles are too stiff for the current exact-hold timestep path.
phase1/runs/task-021-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:92083:- `src/autofdtd/materials/anisotropic.py` now provides `AnisotropicMedium` as the implemented diagonal tensor family plus explicit `FullyAnisotropicMedium` and `Medium2D` defer-policy surfaces; `Medium2D` is parseable and convertible to volumetric `AnisotropicMedium`, but direct simulation use stays rejected in Phase 1.
phase1/runs/task-021-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:92116:- Phase 1 `Sellmeier` support is intentionally passive-only and homogeneous-only: `B_i >= 0`, `C_i >= 0`, zero-`C_i` terms fold into `eps_inf`, and all timestep execution reuses the existing electric-only `PoleResidueMaterialCoefficients` path instead of creating a new auxiliary-state layout.
phase1/runs/task-021-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:92119:- Phase 1 anisotropy stops at diagonal tensor media: `AnisotropicMedium` is implemented and IR-lowered, `FullyAnisotropicMedium` remains an explicit deferred error for runtime compilation, and `Medium2D` remains a deferred direct-simulation feature with offline conversion helpers only.
phase1/runs/task-021-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:92122:- Conductor boundaries are represented as reflection-sign transforms rather than special-casing them inside the future timestep loop: PEC uses odd tangential electric and odd normal magnetic parity, while PMC uses the opposite parity assignment.
