phase1/runs/task-003-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:8568:{"task_id":"task-003","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented a versioned execution IR and bundle serialization contract for Phase 1, including public lowering helpers, manifest-based packaging, schema export, tests, and architecture/docs updates.","key_findings":["Added `autofdtd.ir` models for `ComponentIR`, `StructureIR`, `SceneIR`, `SimulationIR`, `ArtifactIR`, `ExecutionManifestIR`, and `ExecutionPackageIR` under schema version `phase1.v1`.","Lowering from the public container layer is now explicit via `component_to_ir()`, `structure_to_ir()`, `scene_to_ir()`, and `simulation_to_ir()`, keeping the execution IR independent from the API module layout while preserving ordered structure semantics and resolved priorities.","Bundle packaging is directory-based: `manifest.json` records package format `autofdtd.execution-package.v1` and a hashed `simulation.json` entrypoint artifact, avoiding self-referential manifest hashing while remaining suitable for local or remote transport.","Validation now covers the IR schema version, package format, and component envelope basics, and the contract is backed by JSON-schema export plus tests for lowering, bundle writing, and schema inspection."],"artifacts":[{"path":"src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Versioned execution IR models, lowering helpers, bundle writer, and JSON-schema export helpers."},{"path":"src/autofdtd/ir/__init__.py","description":"IR namespace exports for the new execution contract."},{"path":"tests/test_ir.py","description":"Coverage for simulation lowering, bundle serialization, and schema inspection."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","description":"Architecture notes describing the execution IR and packaging contract."},{"path":"phase1/working-memory.md","description":"Updated distilled decisions and handoff notes for later validation and model-base tasks."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"Verification passed with `pytest -q`, `ruff check .`, and `mypy src`. The next tasks can build normalization and shared model-base work on top of the new IR schema/version constants and `ComponentIR` envelope.","next_action":"none"}
