phase1/runs/task-015-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:21948:{"task_id":"task-015","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented passive homogeneous Sellmeier medium support across the public API, typed IR, coefficient compilation, and the shared PoleResidue-family update-kernel path, with examples and validation tests passing.","key_findings":["Added a Phase 1 `Sellmeier` model with `(B_i, C_i)` coefficients, direct `eps_model()` evaluation, passive-subset validation, and single-pole `from_dispersion()` fitting.","Lowered `Sellmeier` into typed `SellmeierIR` while compiling runtime coefficients by converting to an equivalent `PoleResidue`, preserving the public family tag as `medium_type=\"Sellmeier\"`.","Kept runtime support on the existing complex-polarization auxiliary-state layout, so Sellmeier execution reuses `PoleResidueMaterialCoefficients` and `pole_residue_electric_update()` instead of introducing a parallel kernel contract.","Added representative tests for model validation, formula correctness, IR emission, scene compilation, and shared-kernel execution; full test suite now passes."],"artifacts":[{"path":"src/autofdtd/materials/dispersive.py","description":"Added the Sellmeier public model, coefficient validation, direct permittivity evaluation, pole-residue lowering, and passive dispersion fitting helper."},{"path":"src/autofdtd/compiler/materials.py","description":"Added Sellmeier coefficient compilation onto the shared PoleResidue auxiliary-state contract and routed generic medium compilation through it."},{"path":"src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Added typed `SellmeierIR` lowering and medium-IR dispatch support."},{"path":"tests/test_materials.py","description":"Added representative Sellmeier validation, compilation, IR, scene, and kernel-path tests."},{"path":"src/autofdtd/examples/materials.py","description":"Added a Sellmeier compilation example showing public-model, pole-residue lowering, and compiled coefficient outputs."},{"path":"phase1/working-memory.md","description":"Recorded Sellmeier support decisions and the shared runtime-contract choice for later material-family tasks."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"Lorentz, Drude, and Debye can follow the same pattern: keep family-specific public and IR models, but lower onto the existing PoleResidue-family auxiliary-state runtime contract whenever the formulation permits it.","next_action":"none"}
phase1/runs/task-015-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:21976: - `src/autofdtd/materials/dispersive.py` now provides a Phase 1 `PoleResidue` public model with JSON-safe complex-pair storage, causal validation (`Re(a) <= 0`), `eps_model()`, and limited `Medium` conversion helpers.
phase1/runs/task-015-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:21989:+- Phase 1 `Sellmeier` support is intentionally passive-only and homogeneous-only: `B_i >= 0`, `C_i >= 0`, zero-`C_i` terms fold into `eps_inf`, and all timestep execution reuses the existing electric-only `PoleResidueMaterialCoefficients` path instead of creating a new auxiliary-state layout.
