phase1/logs/console.log:325463:phase1/logs/console.log:283884:phase1/runs/task-002-attempt-001/result.json:1:{"task_id":"task-002","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented the first tagged immutable container backbone for `Simulation`, `Scene`, and `Structure`, including ordered structure precedence helpers, name validation, and JSON-ready serialization scaffolding for later IR work.","key_findings":["`src/autofdtd/core/containers.py` now provides frozen pydantic container models with explicit `type` tags, JSON-ready payload helpers, and minimal disk serialization entrypoints.","`Scene` preserves ordered structure semantics and exposes `structures_in_resolution_order()` so later scene compilation can apply structures by resolved priority and insertion order without re-deriving precedence rules.","`StructurePriorityMode.CONDUCTOR` is mapped early using medium type tags so implicit priority behavior can distinguish dielectric, lossy-metal, and PEC structures before concrete material classes land.","`Simulation` now carries the Phase 1 shell fields from the feature checklist, including domain size, run time, sources, monitors, boundary and grid references, symmetry, shutoff, courant, and subpixel references.","Focused tests now cover name normalization, duplicate-name rejection, ordered overlap behavior, conductor-priority defaults, and tagged JSON serialization, and the repo passes `pytest`, `ruff`, and `mypy`."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/core/containers.py","description":"Frozen tagged container models and precedence/serialization helpers for `Structure`, `Scene`, and `Simulation`."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/api/simulation.py","description":"Public API re-exports for the foundational container models."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/api/__init__.py","description":"API namespace exports exposing the new container backbone."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/core/__init__.py","description":"Core namespace exports exposing the tagged container layer."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_containers.py","description":"Container-model tests for names, precedence ordering, conductor priority defaults, and JSON serialization."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/architecture.md","description":"Architecture notes updated to describe the current container backbone and separation from future IR work."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/working-memory.md","description":"Condensed handoff notes capturing the container-model decisions for later tasks."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/loop.spec.md","description":"Task board updated to mark `task-002` completed."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-002-attempt-001/result.json","description":"Recorded task output matching the Phase 1 result schema."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"`task-003` should now define the separate execution IR contract and treat the current container payload helpers as an interim handoff format rather than the final IR schema.","next_action":"none"}
phase1/logs/console.log:325470:phase1/logs/console.log:283897:phase1/runs/task-016-attempt-001/result.json:1:{"task_id":"task-016","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented passive homogeneous Lorentz, damped Drude, and passive homogeneous Debye medium support across the public API, typed IR, coefficient compilation, and the shared PoleResidue-family update path, with explicit tests for each family.","key_findings":["`autofdtd.materials` now exposes `Lorentz`, `Drude`, and `Debye` models with analytical `eps_model()` evaluation, family-specific validation, and lowering to equivalent `PoleResidue` payloads.","`autofdtd.ir` now emits typed `LorentzIR`, `DrudeIR`, and `DebyeIR` payloads, and the compiler preserves the originating family tag while compiling onto the existing `PoleResidueMaterialCoefficients` auxiliary-state contract.","Compilation now fails explicitly when converted dispersive poles are too stiff for the current exact-hold timestep path, which clearly delimits the currently supported subset instead of emitting unusable coefficients.","Examples, docs, tests, and working memory were updated so the new families are exercised and the subset boundary is recorded for later material/runtime tasks."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/materials/dispersive.py","description":"Added Lorentz, Drude, and Debye public models plus analytical-to-PoleResidue lowering helpers."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/materials/__init__.py","description":"Extended Phase 1 medium dispatch and exports to include Lorentz, Drude, and Debye."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/compiler/materials.py","description":"Added Lorentz, Drude, and Debye coefficient compilation on the shared PoleResidue runtime contract plus explicit stiff-pole rejection."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Added typed LorentzIR, DrudeIR, and DebyeIR lowering and medium dispatch integration."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/kernels/materials.py","description":"Updated constitutive metadata so the shared dispersive kernel path reports Lorentz, Drude, and Debye support."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/examples/materials.py","description":"Added compiled analytical-dispersion examples covering Lorentz, Drude, and Debye lowering and coefficient generation."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/materials.md","description":"Documented the added analytical dispersive families and the explicit stiff-pole compile rejection policy."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_materials.py","description":"Added named Lorentz, Drude, and Debye validation, IR, compilation, and shared-kernel tests."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/working-memory.md","description":"Recorded the new analytical-dispersion decisions and the stiff-pole subset boundary for later tasks."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-016-attempt-001/result.json","description":"Recorded the structured task result for this run."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"Verification passed with `ruff check src tests`, `pytest -q tests/test_materials.py`, and `python -m compileall src`. A repo-wide `mypy src` run still reports pre-existing unrelated typing issues outside this task’s scope.","next_action":"none"}
phase1/logs/console.log:325473:phase1/logs/console.log:283904:phase1/runs/task-010-attempt-001/result.json:1:{"task_id":"task-010","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented the Phase 1 manual grid surface with typed `UniformGrid`, `CustomGrid`, `CustomGridBoundaries`, and `GridSpec` models, simulation-time grid resolution, and typed grid IR lowering with resolved boundary metadata.","key_findings":["`src/autofdtd/grid/specs.py` now provides concrete Phase 1 grid models plus `ResolvedGrid`/`ResolvedGridAxis` so simulations can resolve axis boundaries before compiler/runtime work lands.","`Simulation.resolved_grid()` and `core.validation` now enforce a strict top-level `GridSpec` contract, validate manual grid compatibility against simulation bounds, and reject planned-but-not-yet-implemented grid families like `AutoGrid` explicitly.","`src/autofdtd/ir/models.py` now lowers `GridSpec` into typed grid IR (`GridSpecIR`, per-axis IR, and resolved grid metadata), giving later discretization and mode-solver tasks an inspectable execution-side mesh contract.","Public exports, examples, and docs were updated so the grid surface is part of the Tidy3D-inspired API rather than an opaque dict payload.","Verification passed with `python -m ruff check src tests` and `python -m pytest` (47 tests passed)."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/grid/specs.py","description":"Phase 1 manual grid models, resolution helpers, and domain-to-boundary lowering."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/core/containers.py","description":"`Simulation.resolved_grid()` integration and grid-spec validation during simulation construction."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/core/validation.py","description":"Checklist-aware normalization for `GridSpec` and explicit rejection of not-yet-implemented grid families."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Typed grid execution IR and lowering path with resolved grid metadata."},{"path":"/wo