cit.\\n246\\t\\n247\\t## [QUEUED] task-031 - Implement the vector mode solver integration path\\n248\\tSuccess: Introduce a GPU-capable or GPU-ready mode-solver subsystem whose interface is compatible with sampled epsilon tensors over deterministic cross-sections and includes tests for representative cases.\\n249\\tAttempts: 0\\n250\\tLast Run: -\\n251\\tLast Duration: -\\n252\\tCompleted At: -\\n253\\tNotes: Use VectorModesolver.jl as a formulation and interface reference, not as a blind dependency surface. This task intentionally lands before ModeSource and mode-monitor work.\\n254\\t\\n255\\t## [QUEUED] task-032 - Implement ModeSource with solver-backed mode definitions and injection support\\n256\\tSuccess: Support ModeSource with explicit integration into the mode-solver or mode-definition surface, including validation, IR lowering, source planning, injection support, and representative tests.\\n257\\tAttempts: 0\\n258\\tLast Run: -\\n259\\tLast Duration: -\\n260\\tCompleted At: -\\n261\\tNotes: This task comes after the mode solver on purpose so it has a real backend to target.\\n262\\t\\n263\\t## [QUEUED] task-033 - Implement PlaneWave plus angular-spec models and injection support\\n264\\tSuccess: Support PlaneWave along with the angular-spec models it needs, including validation, IR lowering, source planning, injection support, and representative tests.\\n265\\tAttempts: 0\\n266\\tLast Run: -\\n267\\tLast Duration: -\\n268\\tCompleted At: -\\n269\\tNotes: PlaneWave is a core optical source and should not be hidden inside a broader beam-source task.\\n270\\t\\n271\\t## [QUEUED] task-034 - Implement GaussianBeam and AstigmaticGaussianBeam with injection support\\n272\\tSuccess: Support GaussianBeam and AstigmaticGaussianBeam or a clearly delimited subset, including validation, source planning, injection support, and representative tests.\\n273\\tAttempts: 0\\n274\\tLast Run: -\\n275\\tLast Duration: -\\n276\\tCompleted At: -\\n277\\tNotes: Beam sources have e